<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4 Why Does Effective Rank Not Correlate Well with Performance? ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Increasing batch size increases effective rank, without guaranteeing performance improvement.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4 Why Does Effective Rank Not Correlate Well with Performance? ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">High regularization prompts high effective rank, but varied performance</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4 Why Does Effective Rank Not Correlate Well with Performance? ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Learning Rate affects effective rank and performance inconsistently.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" title="In 4 Why Does Effective Rank Not Correlate Well with Performance? ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">High learning rate annealing leads to high effective rank and low performance.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5" title="In 4 Why Does Effective Rank Not Correlate Well with Performance? ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Training on more tokens preserves a high effective rank and high performance.</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_paragraph">
