<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Experimental Details</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Pre-Training Setup</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 3 Does Effective Rank Reliably Predict Model Performance? ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we pre-train a suite of OLMo-style <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Groeneveld and others, 2024</a>)</cite> models using the model configurations of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Magnusson et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
Specifically, all models have 6 layers, 4 attention heads, an MLP ratio of 4, SwiGLU activation, a sequence length of 2048 and a vocabulary of 50304 tokens.
We use RMS LayerNorm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang and Sennrich, 2019</a>)</cite> across all layers and do not use any dropout.
Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Pre-Training Setup ‣ A.1 Experimental Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> details the hidden dimension for all the model sizes and the model-specific learning rates inferred from the <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Porian et al. (2024)</a></cite>’s scaling laws.
We use the raw Pile dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2020</a>)</cite> for pre-training these models, which is tokenized using the allenai/gpt-neox-olmo-dolma-v1_5 tokenizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Soldaini et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
