</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A1.F27" title="Figure 27 ‣ A.3.5 Catastrophic Forgetting Evaluation. ‣ A.3 Extended Discussion: The Impact of Model Geometry on Downstream Performance ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a> and <a href="#A1.F27" title="Figure 27 ‣ A.3.5 Catastrophic Forgetting Evaluation. ‣ A.3 Extended Discussion: The Impact of Model Geometry on Downstream Performance ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a> show in-distribution loss on Pile-10k for models fine-tuned on StarCoder-Python and OpenWebMath, respectively.
Across model sizes, both the effective rank and the cosine similarity computed for the unembedding matrix, as well as the last-token final-layer representations, remain largely constant and therefore provide little signal for predicting catastrophic forgetting.
Interestingly, isotropy <math id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math> is the only metric that exhibits a weak linear relationship with post–fine-tuning loss.
However, models trained with weight decay <math id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math> form a notable exception, displaying very low isotropy while still achieving strong performance.
Regression results in Tables <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.3.5 Catastrophic Forgetting Evaluation. ‣ A.3 Extended Discussion: The Impact of Model Geometry on Downstream Performance ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ A.3.5 Catastrophic Forgetting Evaluation. ‣ A.3 Extended Discussion: The Impact of Model Geometry on Downstream Performance ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Disentangling Geometry, Performance, and Training in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> corroborate these observations, indicating that catastrophic forgetting is largely invariant to the base model’s unembedding and representation geometry.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F27" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20433v1/per_model_all_open_web_math_effective_rank_vs_post_ft_loss.svg" id="A1.F27.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/75;" width="476" height="75"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20433v1/per_model_all_open_web_math_t_cos_vs_post_ft_loss.svg" id="A1.F27.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/58;" width="476" height="58"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20433v1/per_model_all_open_web_math_isotropy_vs_post_ft_loss.svg" id="A1.F27.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/57;" width="476" height="57"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20433v1/per_model_all_open_web_math_last_token_effective_rank_vs_post_ft_loss.svg" id="A1.F27.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/58;" width="476" height="58"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20433v1/per_model_all_open_web_math_last_token_t_cos_vs_post_ft_loss.svg" id="A1.F27.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/57;" width="476" height="57"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F27.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 27</span>: </span><span id="A1.F27.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Extended forgetting evaluation (OpenWebMath) in relation to geometric metrics of the unembedding matrix and last-layer final-token representation.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
